# ============================================================================
# Terraform-specific ignores (scoped to deploy/terraform)
# ============================================================================
# The repo root .gitignore already excludes *.tfstate, *.tfstate.backup and
# .terraform/. This file adds the bits specific to this tree and documents WHY
# each is ignored.

# Real per-env variable files. terraform.tfvars.example IS committed (the
# template); the filled-in terraform.tfvars may contain environment-specific
# values (e.g. your VPN CIDR) and must NOT be committed.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars

# Backend config passed via -backend-config=*.hcl (may name your real bucket).
*.backend.hcl

# Crash logs + plan output files.
crash.log
*.tfplan

# NOTE on lock files: .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed, one per root module
# (environments/<env>/, bootstrap/). It records the exact provider version
# `terraform init` selected inside the ~> constraints AND the checksums of that
# build for every platform we run on, so a provider binary that does not match
# the recorded hash fails `init` instead of running. After changing a
# constraint, regenerate it with:
#   terraform providers lock -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=darwin_arm64
# (linux_amd64 = CI runners, darwin_arm64 = maintainer laptops.) Dependabot's
# terraform ecosystem updates the lock file together with the constraint.
